       "s": "IT was a summer evening,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Old Kaspar’s work was done,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And he before his cottage door",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Was sitting in the sun;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And by him sported on the green",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "His little grandchild Wilhelmine.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 732,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "She saw her brother Peterkin",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Roll something large and round",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Which he beside the rivulet",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "In playing there had found;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "He came to ask what he had found",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "That was so large and smooth and round.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 732,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Old Kaspar took it from the boy",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Who stood expectant by;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And then the old man shook his head,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And with a natural sigh",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "‘’Tis some poor fellow’s skull,’ said he.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "‘Who fell in the great victory.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 733,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "‘I find them in the garden,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For there’s many here about;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And often when I go to plough",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The ploughshare turns them out.",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "For many thousand men,’ said he,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "‘Were slain in that great victory.’",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 733,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "‘Now tell us what ’twas all about,’",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Young Peterkin he cries;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And little Wilhelmine looks up",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "With wonder-waiting eyes;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "‘Now tell us all about the war,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And what they fought each other for.’",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 733,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "‘It was the English,’ Kaspar cried,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "‘Who put the French to rout;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "But what they fought each other for",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "I could not well make out.",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "But everybody said,’ quoth he,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "‘That ’twas a famous victory.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 733,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "‘My father lived at Blenheim then,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Yon little stream hard by;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "They burnt his dwelling to the ground,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And he was forced to fly:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "So with his wife and child he fled,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Nor had he where to rest his head.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 733,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "‘With fire and sword the country round",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Was wasted far and wide,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And many a childing mother then",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And newborn baby died:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "But things like that, you know, must be",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "At every famous victory.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 733,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "‘They say it was a shocking sight",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "After the field was won;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "For many thousand bodies here",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Lay rotting in the sun:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "But things like that, you know, must be",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "After a famous victory.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 734,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "‘Great praise the Duke of Marlbro’ won",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And our good Prince Eugene;’",
